cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use mestra in published work, please cite it as below, and
  name the specification version your files declare (the root
  attribute `format`, for example "mestra/0").
title: "mestra: an open container for simulation and surrogate data"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Bijective Systems"
repository-code: "https://github.com/bijective-systems-org/mestra"
url: "https://github.com/bijective-systems-org/mestra"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  mestra is an open file format for the data of a parametric or
  time-dependent simulation study and for the surrogate models fitted
  to it. One HDF5 file, laid out to be a valid netCDF-4 file, holds the
  rows of a study with keys that carry roles (design, condition, time,
  group, split, status), scalars with units, fields on a shared mesh
  or axis, uncertainty, and fitted models as callables; a validator
  checks what the file claims. Readers and writers in Python, C++,
  MATLAB and Julia are held to one specification and a shared
  conformance corpus.
keywords:
  - simulation data
  - surrogate model
  - parametric study
  - HDF5
  - netCDF-4
  - mesh
  - scientific machine learning
  - uncertainty quantification
